<title>BRAZIL: Noroeste says sale was a growth strategy.</title>
<headline>Noroeste says sale was a growth strategy.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Banco Noroeste said the sale of a controlling stake to Spain's Banco Santander SA was part of the bank's strategy to grow and become more competitive.</p>
<p>&quot;It was a strategic decision by the controlling shareholders to seek partners to become stronger and more competitive,&quot; said Jayme Marques de Souza, Market Relations director at Banco Noroeste.</p>
<p>Santander on Friday announced its Brazilian unit Banco Geral do Comercio would buy a 50 percent controlling stake in Noroeste for an estimated $500 million.</p>
